TRANSLATED:
The theorem restated in terms of fundamental groups is:

**Theorem:** Let \(X\) and \(Y\) be based topological spaces. If \(\pi_1(X)\) is free and \(\pi_1(X) \cong \pi_1(Y)\), then \(\pi_1(Y)\) is free.

\boxed{\text{Let } X \text{ and } Y \text{ be based topological spaces. If } \pi_1(X) \text{ is free and } \pi_1(X) \cong \pi_1(Y), \text{ then } \pi_1(Y) \text{ is free.}}
